`Choices` inherits from Python's standard `enum.Enum`. In `enum.Enum`, `__str__()` returns `"ClassName.MEMBER_NAME"` (e.g. `'MyChoice.FIRST_CHOICE'`) instead of the enum member's underlying value. When model fields are assigned `TextChoices` or `IntegerChoices` enum members in memory, `str()` on those fields evaluates `enum.Enum.__str__()` and returns the enum representation `'MyChoice.FIRST_CHOICE'` rather than the string representation of its value `'first'`.

